    "result_text": "Both findings were valid and I addressed them; tests remain green.\n\n**Finding 1 (duplicated `normalize`)** \u2014 Agreed. Extracted name normalization into a new shared helper `OwnerNames` (same convention as `OwnerEmails`/`OwnerTelephones`/`Households`), and pointed both `CountNamesakes` and `FlagPossibleDuplicate` at it. I kept the exact prior semantics (`trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT)`, no whitespace-collapse) rather than reusing `Households.normalize`, which additionally collapses internal whitespace \u2014 a subtly different rule that would have silently changed namesake-counting behaviour. The single source of truth now lives in one place for both consumers.\n\n**Finding 2 (`equalsTelephone` reinvents `Objects.equals`)** \u2014 Agreed. Dropped the private helper and used `java.util.Objects.equals(telephone, existing.getTelephone())`.\n\nFull suite: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `AcceptanceTest` green.",
